# continuity — the hour moves on, and the phase carries on
#
# A wait on the Test Bench moves the hour, but not the party, so its CONTINUE does not close the phase
# (NarrativeController.ContinueNarrationSegment): a line marks the new hour, and the text above stays
# live. The wait is spent at the hour it was made, and can be offered again at the next — the bench
# is thought about twice, and a second wait is offered.
#
# The farmer is the Test Yard's one walker: here at dawn, in the wood through the morning and noon,
# back at afternoon. Waited out to the afternoon, he comes into view while the phase carries on, and
# is observed then, in a block added to the live text — nobody narrated him at dawn, since
# --observe-only pins the opening to the bench.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Yard" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Bench"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy succeed
goal sit_and_wait
advance 12 180

# --- the first wait: dawn to morning (advance takes the next hour when the box asks) ---------
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect Time passes:

click button
wait
advance 12 180
expect-not after trying to
expect It is morning now.
expect-state actions action 0 verb=sit_and_wait state=spent
expect-not farmer

# --- the second wait, offered again at the new hour: morning to afternoon --------------------
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose ripelore
advance 12 180
expect-state actions action 1 verb=sit_and_wait state=live
click action 1
choose 0
wait
click continue
wait
click period afternoon
advance 12 180
expect Time passes:

click button
wait
advance 12 180
expect-not after trying to
expect It is afternoon now.
expect-state actions action 1 verb=sit_and_wait state=spent
# The farmer, back from the wood, observed as he comes into view.
expect farmer
quit
